    // Intro
    'Race conditions are a common type of vulnerability closely related to business logic flaws. They occur when websites process requests concurrently without adequate safeguards. This can lead to multiple distinct threads interacting with the same data at the same time, resulting in a "collision" that causes unintended behavior in the application. A race condition attack uses carefully timed requests to cause intentional collisions and exploit this unintended behavior for malicious purposes.' => 'Race condition adalah kerentanan yang berkaitan erat dengan cacat logika bisnis ketika aplikasi memproses beberapa permintaan secara bersamaan tanpa penguncian yang memadai, sehingga terjadi tabrakan pemrosesan atas data yang sama.',
    'The period of time during which a collision is possible is known as the "race window". This could be the fraction of a second between two interactions with the database, for example.' => 'Rentang waktu singkat ketika tabrakan tersebut masih mungkin terjadi disebut "race window", sering kali hanya berlangsung sepersekian detik.',
    'Like other logic flaws, the impact of a race condition is heavily dependent on the application and the specific functionality in which it occurs.' => 'Layaknya cacat logika lainnya, dampak race condition sangat bergantung pada fitur yang terdampak.',
    "In this section, you'll learn how to identify and exploit different types of race condition. We'll teach you how Burp Suite's built-in tooling can help you to overcome the challenges of performing classic attacks, plus a tried and tested methodology that enables you to detect novel classes of race condition in hidden multi-step processes. These go far beyond the limit overruns that you may be familiar with already." => 'Pada bagian ini, Anda akan mempelajari teknik mendeteksi dan mengeksploitasi berbagai kelas race condition, termasuk metode sinkronisasi permintaan paralel dan metodologi menyingkap proses multitahap tersembunyi.',
    "As usual, we've also provided a number of deliberately vulnerable labs that you can use to practice what you've learned safely against realistic targets. Many of these are based on original SecDevLab research, first presented at Black Hat USA 2023." => 'Tersedia pula lab interaktif untuk mempraktikkan berbagai skenario eksploitasi berdasarkan temuan riset yang dipresentasikan pada Black Hat USA 2023.',
    'For more details, check out the accompanying whitepaper: [[A0]]Smashing the state machine: The true potential of web race conditions[[/A0]]' => 'Untuk detail lebih dalam, baca makalah [[A0]]Smashing the state machine: The true potential of web race conditions[[/A0]].',

    // Limit overrun
    'Limit overrun race conditions' => 'Race condition pelampauan batas (limit overrun)',
    'The most well-known type of race condition enables you to exceed some kind of limit imposed by the business logic of the application.' => 'Jenis race condition paling populer adalah limit overrun, yang memungkinkan pengguna melampaui batasan pemakaian atau saldo yang ditetapkan logika bisnis.',
    'For example, consider an online store that lets you enter a promotional code during checkout to get a one-time discount on your order. To apply this discount, the application may perform the following high-level steps:' => 'Sebagai ilustrasi, toko daring yang mengizinkan kode kupon sekali pakai menjalankan alur berikut saat checkout:',
    "Check that you haven't already used this code." => 'Memeriksa apakah pengguna belum pernah memakai kode tersebut.',
    'Apply the discount to the order total.' => 'Menerapkan potongan harga ke total belanja.',
    "Update the record in the database to reflect the fact that you've now used this code." => 'Memperbarui basis data untuk menandai bahwa kode sudah dipakai.',
    'If you later attempt to reuse this code, the initial checks performed at the start of the process should prevent you from doing this:' => 'Pada penggunaan ulang secara normal, pemeriksaan awal langsung menolak kode promo tersebut:',
    'Now consider what would happen if a user who has never applied this discount code before tried to apply it twice at almost exactly the same time:' => 'Namun perhatikan jika dua permintaan memakai kode tersebut dikirim hampir bersamaan sebelum penanda di basis data sempat diperbarui:',
    "As you can see, the application transitions through a temporary sub-state; that is, a state that it enters and then exits again before request processing is complete. In this case, the sub-state begins when the server starts processing the first request, and ends when it updates the database to indicate that you've already used this code. This introduces a small race window during which you can repeatedly claim the discount as many times as you like." => 'Selama jendela sempit di sub-status sebelum basis data diperbarui, pemeriksaan awal masih menganggap kupon belum dipakai sehingga diskon dapat diklaim berkali-kali.',
