    // Hidden multi-step & methodology
    'Hidden multi-step sequences' => 'Rangkaian multitahap tersembunyi',
    'In practice, a single request may initiate an entire multi-step sequence behind the scenes, transitioning the application through multiple hidden states that it enters and then exits again before request processing is complete. We\'ll refer to these as "sub-states".' => 'Satu permintaan HTTP kerap memicu beberapa tahapan internal (sub-state) sebelum selesai membalas respons.',
    'If you can identify one or more HTTP requests that cause an interaction with the same data, you can potentially abuse these sub-states to expose time-sensitive variations of the kinds of logic flaws that are common in multi-step workflows. This enables race condition exploits that go far beyond limit overruns.' => 'Jika permintaan lain menyentuh data yang sama saat sub-state berlangsung, penyerang dapat memicu celah logika sensitif waktu.',
    'For example, you may be familiar with flawed multi-factor authentication (MFA) workflows that let you perform the first part of the login using known credentials, then navigate straight to the application via forced browsing, effectively bypassing MFA entirely.' => 'Sebagai contoh, perhatikan celah alur login MFA ketika sesi pengguna sudah dibuat lebih dulu sebelum penanda penegakan MFA diaktifkan:',
    "If you're not familiar with this exploit, check out the 2FA simple bypass lab in our Authentication vulnerabilities topic." => 'Jika belum familier dengan pola ini, tinjau kembali materi bypass 2FA pada topik kerentanan autentikasi.',
    'The following pseudo-code demonstrates how a website could be vulnerable to a race variation of this attack:' => 'Pseudocode berikut menggambarkan celah sub-state sementara tersebut:',
    "As you can see, this is in fact a multi-step sequence within the span of a single request. Most importantly, it transitions through a sub-state in which the user temporarily has a valid logged-in session, but MFA isn't yet being enforced. An attacker could potentially exploit this by sending a login request along with a request to a sensitive, authenticated endpoint." => 'Dalam sepersekian detik sebelum baris penegakan MFA dieksekusi, sesi sudah berstatus masuk tanpa syarat MFA sehingga permintaan paralel ke halaman terautentikasi berhasil menembusnya.',
    "We'll look at some more examples of hidden multi-step sequences later, and you'll be able to practice exploiting them in our interactive labs. However, as these vulnerabilities are quite application-specific, it's important to first understand the broader methodology you'll need to apply in order to identify them efficiently, both in the labs and in the wild." => 'Mari pelajari metodologi terstruktur untuk menemukan race condition tersembunyi di target nyata.',
    'Methodology' => 'Metodologi',
    'To detect and exploit hidden multi-step sequences, we recommend the following methodology, which is summarized from the whitepaper [[A0]]Smashing the state machine: The true potential of web race conditions[[/A0]] by SecDevLab Research.' => 'Untuk mendeteksi sub-state tersembunyi, terapkan metodologi tiga langkah berikut dari makalah [[A0]]Smashing the state machine: The true potential of web race conditions[[/A0]]:',
    '1 - Predict potential collisions' => '1 - Prediksi potensi tabrakan',
    'Testing every endpoint is impractical. After mapping out the target site as normal, you can reduce the number of endpoints that you need to test by asking yourself the following questions:' => 'Daripada menguji seluruh situs, saring endpoint yang paling berisiko melalui dua pertanyaan ini:',
    '<strong>Is this endpoint security critical?</strong> Many endpoints don\'t touch critical functionality, so they\'re not worth testing.' => '<strong>Apakah endpoint ini menyentuh fitur krusial?</strong> Fokus pada autentikasi, keuangan, hak akses, atau perubahan identitas.',
    '<strong>Is there any collision potential?</strong> For a successful collision, you typically need two or more requests that trigger operations on the same record. For example, consider the following variations of a password reset implementation:' => '<strong>Apakah ada potensi tabrakan atas data yang sama?</strong> Tabrakan terjadi jika dua permintaan memanipulasi rekaman data yang sama.',
    'With the first example, requesting parallel password resets for two different users is unlikely to cause a collision as it results in changes to two different records. However, the second implementation enables you to edit the same record with requests for two different users.' => 'Jika token atur ulang kata sandi disimpan per sesi, bukan per akun pengguna di basis data, dua permintaan berbeda dalam satu sesi akan saling menimpa.',
    '2 - Probe for clues' => '2 - Uji untuk menemukan petunjuk',
    'To recognize clues, you first need to benchmark how the endpoint behaves under normal conditions. You can do this in Burp Repeater by grouping all of your requests and using the <strong>Send group in sequence (separate connections)</strong> option. For more information, see [[A0]]Sending requests in sequence[[/A0]].' => 'Lakukan tolok ukur perilaku normal terlebih dahulu memakai pengiriman berurutan ([[A0]]Mengirim permintaan berurutan[[/A0]]).',
    "Next, send the same group of requests at once using the single-packet attack (or last-byte sync if HTTP/2 isn't supported) to minimize network jitter. You can do this in Burp Repeater by selecting the <strong>Send group in parallel</strong> option. For more information, see [[A0]]Sending requests in parallel[[/A0]]. Alternatively, you can use the Turbo Intruder extension, which is available from the [[A1]]BApp Store[[/A1]]." => 'Selanjutnya kirim grup permintaan yang sama secara paralel menggunakan single-packet attack atau ekstensi di [[A1]]BApp Store[[/A1]] (lihat [[A0]]Mengirim permintaan secara paralel[[/A0]]).',
    "Anything at all can be a clue. Just look for some form of deviation from what you observed during benchmarking. This includes a change in one or more responses, but don't forget second-order effects like different email contents or a visible change in the application's behavior afterward." => 'Bandingkan hasilnya terhadap tolok ukur normal; perhatikan perubahan kode status, isi email notifikasi, atau perilaku akun setelahnya.',
    '<label class="label-edition is-professional">Professional</label> To test for race condition vulnerabilities quickly and easily, you can use the [[A0]]Trigger race conditions[[/A0]] custom action. This sends parallel requests with a single click, removing the need to manually create and group tabs in Repeater.' => '<label class="label-edition is-professional">Professional</label> Pengujian race condition juga dapat dipercepat dengan aksi khusus [[A0]]Trigger race conditions[[/A0]] untuk mengirim permintaan paralel satu klik.',
    'For more information about how to use custom actions, see [[A0]]Custom actions[[/A0]].' => 'Pelajari pemakaian aksi kustom pada [[A0]]Custom actions[[/A0]].',
    '3 - Prove the concept' => '3 - Buktikan konsep serangan',
    "Try to understand what's happening, remove superfluous requests, and make sure you can still replicate the effects." => 'Pahami mekanisme di balik layar, kurangi permintaan yang tidak perlu, dan pastikan efeknya dapat direproduksi secara konsisten.',
    "Advanced race conditions can cause unusual and unique primitives, so the path to maximum impact isn't always immediately obvious. It may help to think of each race condition as a structural weakness rather than an isolated vulnerability." => 'Perlakukan race condition sebagai celah struktural alih-alih bug tunggal agar Anda dapat memaksimalkan dampak akhirnya.',
    'For a more detailed methodology, check out the full whitepaper: [[A0]]Smashing the state machine: The true potential of web race conditions[[/A0]]' => 'Untuk metodologi lengkapnya, baca [[A0]]Smashing the state machine: The true potential of web race conditions[[/A0]].',

    // Multi & Single endpoint
    'Multi-endpoint race conditions' => 'Race condition multi-endpoint',
    'Perhaps the most intuitive form of these race conditions are those that involve sending requests to multiple endpoints at the same time.' => 'Bentuk yang cukup intuitif adalah memanggil dua endpoint berbeda secara bersamaan.',
    'Think about the classic logic flaw in online stores where you add an item to your basket or cart, pay for it, then add more items to the cart before force-browsing to the order confirmation page.' => 'Bayangkan alur toko daring saat pembayaran diproses: menambah barang ke keranjang tepat di antara pemeriksaan pembayaran dan konfirmasi pesanan.',
    "If you're not familiar with this exploit, check out the Insufficient workflow validation lab from our Business logic vulnerabilities topic." => 'Jika belum familier, lihat lab validasi alur kerja pada topik kerentanan logika bisnis.',
    'A variation of this vulnerability can occur when payment validation and order confirmation are performed during the processing of a single request. The state machine for the order status might look something like this:' => 'Variasi race condition terjadi ketika verifikasi pembayaran dan konfirmasi pesanan berjalan dalam satu permintaan yang sama:',
    'In this case, you can potentially add more items to your basket during the race window between when the payment is validated and when the order is finally confirmed.' => 'Permintaan paralel untuk menambah produk berpotensi menyelipkan barang gratis sesudah nilai pembayaran divalidasi.',
    'Aligning multi-endpoint race windows' => 'Menyelaraskan jendela waktu multi-endpoint',
    'When testing for multi-endpoint race conditions, you may encounter issues trying to line up the race windows for each request, even if you send them all at exactly the same time using the single-packet technique.' => 'Pada skenario multi-endpoint, waktu pemrosesan tiap endpoint sering berbeda sehingga race window tidak langsung sejajar.',
    'This common problem is primarily caused by the following two factors:' => 'Penyebab utamanya terbagi menjadi dua faktor berikut:',
    '<strong>Delays introduced by network architecture -</strong> For example, there may be a delay whenever the front-end server establishes a new connection to the back-end. The protocol used can also have a major impact.' => '<strong>Jeda arsitektur jaringan -</strong> Misalnya keterlambatan saat frontend membuka koneksi baru ke backend.',
    '<strong>Delays introduced by endpoint-specific processing -</strong> Different endpoints inherently vary in their processing times, sometimes significantly so, depending on what operations they trigger.' => '<strong>Jeda pemrosesan khusus endpoint -</strong> Setiap endpoint memiliki durasi eksekusi yang berbeda bergantung pada beban kerjanya.',
    'Fortunately, there are potential workarounds to both of these issues.' => 'Kedua kendala waktu tersebut dapat diatasi dengan teknik berikut.',
    'Connection warming' => 'Pemanasan koneksi (connection warming)',
    "Back-end connection delays don't usually interfere with race condition attacks because they typically delay parallel requests equally, so the requests stay in sync." => 'Keterlambatan koneksi backend biasanya menunda semua permintaan paralel secara merata.',
    "It's essential to be able to distinguish these delays from those caused by endpoint-specific factors. One way to do this is by \"warming\" the connection with one or more inconsequential requests to see if this smoothes out the remaining processing times. In Burp Repeater, you can try adding a [[C0]] request for the homepage to the start of your tab group, then using the <strong>Send group in sequence (single connection)</strong> option." => 'Anda dapat memanaskan koneksi terlebih dahulu dengan menambahkan permintaan [[C0]] ringan ke beranda sebelum urutan serangan utama.',
    'If the first request still has a longer processing time, but the rest of the requests are now processed within a short window, you can ignore the apparent delay and continue testing as normal.' => 'Jika permintaan pemanasan pertama saja yang lambat sedangkan sisanya seragam dan cepat, koneksi sudah siap dipakai menyerang.',
    'If you still see inconsistent response times on a single endpoint, even when using the single-packet technique, this is an indication that the back-end delay is interfering with your attack. You may be able to work around this by using Turbo Intruder to send some connection warming requests before following up with your main attack requests.' => 'Jika latensi masih acak, gunakan Turbo Intruder untuk mengirim beberapa permintaan pemanas sebelum melepaskan gerbang serangan utama.',
    'Abusing rate or resource limits' => 'Menyalahgunakan pembatasan laju atau sumber daya',
    "If connection warming doesn't make any difference, there are various solutions to this problem." => 'Bila pemanasan koneksi tidak membantu, ada cara lain untuk menyamakan waktu tiba di server.',
    "Using Turbo Intruder, you can introduce a short client-side delay. However, as this involves splitting your actual attack requests across multiple TCP packets, you won't be able to use the single-packet attack technique. As a result, on high-jitter targets, the attack is unlikely to work reliably regardless of what delay you set." => 'Menambahkan jeda dari sisi klien memisahkan paket TCP sehingga rentan gagal bila jitter jaringan tinggi.',
    'Instead, you may be able to solve this problem by abusing a common security feature.' => 'Solusi yang lebih andal justru berasal dari penyalahgunaan fitur pembatasan laju di sisi server.',
    'Web servers often delay the processing of requests if too many are sent too quickly. By sending a large number of dummy requests to intentionally trigger the rate or resource limit, you may be able to cause a suitable server-side delay. This makes the single-packet attack viable even when delayed execution is required.' => 'Mengirimkan banyak permintaan pancingan bersama satu paket serangan dapat memicu penundaan pemrosesan di server untuk menyelaraskan waktu eksekusi endpoint.',
    'Single-endpoint race conditions' => 'Race condition pada satu endpoint',
    'Sending parallel requests with different values to a single endpoint can sometimes trigger powerful race conditions.' => 'Mengirim permintaan paralel dengan parameter berbeda ke satu endpoint yang sama dapat memicu tabrakan status.',
