    'Time-sensitive attacks' => 'Serangan sensitif waktu',
    'Sometimes you may not find race conditions, but the techniques for delivering requests with precise timing can still reveal the presence of other vulnerabilities.' => 'Meskipun tabrakan konkurensi tidak ada, teknik pengiriman serentak tetap efektif menyingkap kelemahan pembuatan token acak.',
    'One such example is when high-resolution timestamps are used instead of cryptographically secure random strings to generate security tokens.' => 'Contohnya ketika token keamanan diturunkan dari stempel waktu (timestamp) alih-alih generator acak kriptografis.',
    'Consider a password reset token that is only randomized using a timestamp. In this case, it might be possible to trigger two password resets for two different users, which both use the same token. All you need to do is time the requests so that they generate the same timestamp.' => 'Mengirim dua permintaan reset secara bersamaan untuk akun berbeda berpotensi menghasilkan nilai token reset yang identik.',
    'How to prevent race condition vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan race condition',
    'When a single request can transition an application through invisible sub-states, understanding and predicting its behavior is extremely difficult. This makes defense impractical. To secure an application properly, we recommend eliminating sub-states from all sensitive endpoints by applying the following strategies:' => 'Hilangkan sub-status sementara pada seluruh endpoint sensitif dengan menerapkan langkah-langkah berikut:',
    'Avoid mixing data from different storage places.' => 'Hindari pencampuran penyimpanan status antara lapisan sesi dan basis data utama.',
    "Ensure sensitive endpoints make state changes atomic by using the datastore's concurrency features. For example, use a single database transaction to check the payment matches the cart value and confirm the order." => 'Gunakan transaksi basis data yang atomik untuk memeriksa syarat dan memperbarui status dalam satu operasi utuh.',
    'As a defense-in-depth measure, take advantage of datastore integrity and consistency features like column uniqueness constraints.' => 'Manfaatkan batasan integritas basis data seperti constraint keunikan kolom (unique constraints).',
    "Don't attempt to use one data storage layer to secure another. For example, sessions aren't suitable for preventing limit overrun attacks on databases." => 'Jangan mengandalkan penguncian di satu lapisan penyimpanan untuk melindungi lapisan penyimpanan lainnya.',
    'Ensure your session handling framework keeps sessions internally consistent. Updating session variables individually instead of in a batch might be a tempting optimization, but it\'s extremely dangerous. This goes for ORMs too; by hiding away concepts like transactions, they\'re taking on full responsibility for them.' => 'Pastikan pembaruan sesi maupun transaksi ORM menjaga konsistensi status secara penuh tanpa kondisi parsial.',
    "In some architectures, it may be appropriate to avoid server-side state entirely. Instead, you could use encryption to push the state client-side, for example, using JWTs. Note that this has its own risks, as we've covered extensively in our topic on [[A0]]JWT attacks[[/A0]]." => 'Pada arsitektur tertentu, status dapat dipindahkan ke sisi klien memakai token terenkripsi atau bertanda tangan seperti [[A0]]JWT[[/A0]] dengan pengamanan semestinya.',
